W: tell me, bright little babbling brooklet
W: whither do you go?
W: tell, Ah! 
W: tell me whence you come
W: and why do you hurry so?
W: pure and bright
W: through the rdiant night
W: happy all through the day
W: gossipping along
W: to your own sweet song
W: I wonder what you say
W: I will try 
W: was the brooks reply
W: to answer your questions three
W: I come from the rills
W: of the far off hills
W: and go to the boundless sea
W: the rocks are  strong 
W: and the way is long
W: so you see why I haste
W: gossipping along
W: to my own sweet song
W: I have no time to waste
W: lo! we see 
W: in the babbling brooklet
W: type of the human soul
W: God above is the hidden source
W: eternity the goal
W: the foes are strong 
W: and the way is long
W: life by work is embraced
W: live it, if you can
W: on the brooklet's plan
W: you have no time to waste
W: no time to waste

